<title>BELGIUM: EU restores pigmeat export refunds.</title>
<headline>EU restores pigmeat export refunds.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Tuesday reintroduced refunds of 10 Ecus per 100 kg on exports of fresh and frozen pigmeat to all destinations, a Commission spokesman said.</p>
<p>The move was aimed at restoring market stability after a recent 25 Ecus per 100 kg fall in prices.</p>
<p>Due to cheap pigmeat prices, refunds on exports of products, such as sausages and ham, were halved, representing a cut of five to 10 Ecus per 100 kg.</p>
</text>
